      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No, butter or oil should never be used on burns because they can bake the burn deeper into the skin and significantly increase your risk of infection. For home care, you can apply a thin layer of plain, sterile petrolatum to keep the wound moist, but this does not replace the need for professional medical evaluation. Given the presence of blisters and severe pain, it is strongly recommended that you see a doctor immediately to get appropriate pain management and prevent complications.",
