      "content": "While aloe vera can soothe minor skin irritations, applying it to a chemical burn may be dangerous as it contains salicylate which can interfere with topical drug absorption, and it is not considered a reliable or standard treatment for significant thermal injuries. Since the burn is already blistering and requires medical evaluation for pain management, trying to self-treat with aloe might lead to worsening infection or delayed healing. Please prioritize seeing a doctor immediately to ensure the blister doesn't get infected and to get appropriate care for the pain.",
